From: aiueo52 <aiueo52@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 21:41:43 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 066/105] adaptive: re-seed the EMA on step-down only; ship the
 validated config

The residual churn after the draft-extend fix (24 switches/run) was
agent-loop oscillating at the step-up boundary: it measures 2.29 accepted
drafts at steps=3 but arrives there carrying a steps=15 EMA of ~4.4, and a
20-batch window is not long enough to forget it, so it steps straight back
up. Re-seeding at the new neutral value fixes that -- but only downward:
seeding at 14 on a step UP makes every workload look worth 15 steps for a
window, which is what made v1 switch 489 times in 90 s.

reset_ema_on_switch now takes false / true / "down". Shipped config: alpha
0.07, interval 20, grace 40, step-down at EMA <= 5.0, step-up at > 2.5,
down-only reseed. 24 -> 10 switches per benchmark.

Validated 21:31-21:40, one window, repeats=2, needle PASS on all three:

  workload     W4           W16          adaptive     vs better fixed
  code-edit    3.88 / 318   11.55 / 528  8.98 / 463   -12%
  prose-en     2.57 / 220    3.10 / 156  2.54 / 229    +4%
  prose-ja     2.29 / 208    3.31 / 170  2.25 / 205    -1%
  agent-loop   3.19 / 282    4.87 / 235  4.05 / 306    +9%

One server now replaces the hand-picked profile: +46% over W4 on code-edit
and +47/+21/+30% over W16 on prose-en/prose-ja/agent-loop; agent-loop beats
both fixed profiles because the controller mixes them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
